-- Rules of Court 2021 (Singapore), G.N. No. S 914/2021, current version as at 5 November 2026.
-- ORDER 18, DIVISION 1: APPEALS -- GENERAL, rules 1 to 14 (roc3, layer 1).
-- Source: a plain-text rendering made by a converter script from Singapore Statutes Online.
-- It is not the official text, and nothing here has been checked against the official text.
--
-- HOW TO READ A RESULT.  A decision function answers `MAYBE BOOLEAN` (or `MAYBE DATE`).
--   JUST TRUE / a date   the text says yes (or names the date) on these facts.
--   JUST FALSE           the text says no in its own words: a flat negative, "only", a period it
--                        fixes in its own words that has run out, an "if", "where" or "unless" read
--                        as the text's no.
--   NOTHING              the text does not answer: it limits a grant by its own wording (a scope with
--                        no "only", a manner, a complement), is silent, or points outside the sources.
-- A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.
-- THE POLARITY OF "UNLESS": for a requirement ("must be ... unless the Court otherwise orders") a
-- direction that the text allows makes the answer JUST FALSE (the requirement does not apply); for a
-- prohibition ("no oral arguments are to be made unless ...") it makes the answer NOTHING (the
-- prohibition lapses and the paragraph does not say that the thing is allowed).  Fork 18.1.
-- TIME.  A period is a constant of the core type `Period`; timeliness is decided against the input
-- `o 3 r 3 the last day for doing the act` (PLAN.md 5.1, S-T1).  O 3 r 2(1) is not threaded.
-- The appellate Court, the lower Court, the Judge and the Registrar are named by the Rules' own words
-- (O 1 r 3(1)); where the outcome does not turn on which decision-maker sits, the input is a fact.

-- ===========================================================================
§ `Order 18 -- Appeals, Division 1 -- General (rules 1 to 14)`
-- ===========================================================================

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 1 -- scope of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 18 r 1(1) kind of proceeding` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(i) an appeal from a decision made on an application in an action`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(ii) an appeal from a decision made on an appeal against a decision mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(iii) an appeal from a decision made on an appeal against a decision mentioned in sub-paragraph (ii)`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(iv) an appeal from a decision made by the Registrar other than a decision mentioned in sub-paragraph (i)`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(iv a) an appeal from a decision made by a District Judge or Magistrate in a hearing on the merits of an originating application`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(a)(v) an appeal from a decision of an appellate Court on an application by summons in an appeal under this Order or Order 19`
    `o 18 r 1(1)(b) an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal to the appellate Court under this Order`
    `o 18 r 1(1) any other proceeding`

-- src:1699 | 1. —(1) This Order applies to and in relation to — ( a )
-- src:1700 | every appeal from — (i)
-- src:1701 | a decision made on an application in an action;
-- src:1702 | (ii)
-- src:1703 | a decision made on an appeal against a decision mentioned in sub‑paragraph (i);
-- src:1704 | (iii)
-- src:1705 | a decision made on an appeal against a decision mentioned in sub‑paragraph (ii);
-- src:1706 | (iv)
-- src:1707 | a decision made by the Registrar other than a decision mentioned in sub-paragraph (i), including a decision made on an assessment of damages or the taking of accounts, or in a hearing on the merits of an originating application; [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1708 | (iv a )
-- src:1709 | a decision made by a District Judge or Magistrate in a hearing on the merits of an originating application, including any application taken out or heard on the same day as such hearing or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the decision; or [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1710 | (v)
-- src:1711 | a decision of an appellate Court on an application by summons in an appeal under this Order or Order 19; and
-- src:1712 | ( b )
-- src:1713 | an application to the appellate Court relating to an appeal to the appellate Court under this Order.
@ref O 18 r 1(1) (src:1699-1713)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 1(1) kind of proceeding`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 1(1) this Order applies to the proceeding` MEANS
    IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 1(1) any other proceeding`
    THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): "This Order applies to and in relation to" the listed appeals and applications; the paragraph does not say that it applies to nothing else
    ELSE JUST TRUE

DECLARE `o 18 r 1(2) kind of application` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 1(2)(a)(i) an application taken out after the action is commenced`
    `o 18 r 1(2)(a)(ii) an application made for a consequential or incidental matter after judgment is given in the trial of an originating claim or the hearing on the merits in an originating application`
    `o 18 r 1(2)(a)(iii) an application for the enforcement of the judgment or order`
    `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(i) an application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment`
    `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(ii) a matter under appeal which is within the scope of Order 19`
    `o 18 r 1(2) any other application`

-- src:1714 | (2) In this Order, an application in an action — ( a )
-- src:1715 | includes any application — (i)
-- src:1716 | taken out after the action is commenced;
-- src:1717 | (ii)
-- src:1718 | made for any consequential or incidental matter after judgment is given in the trial of an originating claim or the hearing on the merits in an originating application; or
-- src:1719 | (iii)
-- src:1720 | for the enforcement of the judgment or order; and
-- src:1721 | ( b )
-- src:1722 | excludes — (i)
-- src:1723 | any application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment (except an application mentioned in paragraph (1)( a )(iv a )); and [S 206/2022 wef 01/04/2022]
-- src:1724 | (ii)
-- src:1725 | any matter under appeal which is within the scope of Order 19.
@ref O 18 r 1(2) (src:1714-1725)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 1(2) kind of application`
      `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (1)(a)(iv a)` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 1(2) the application is an application in an action` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(i) an application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment` AND `it is an application mentioned in paragraph (1)(a)(iv a)` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "(except an application mentioned in paragraph (1)(a)(iv a))" (the exclusion is lifted; the paragraph does not say the application is then included)
        IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(i) an application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application, or at any time after the commencement of such hearing until the giving of the judgment` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "excludes — (i) any application taken out or heard on the same day as the hearing on the merits of an originating claim or an originating application"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 1(2)(b)(ii) a matter under appeal which is within the scope of Order 19` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "excludes — ... any matter under appeal which is within the scope of Order 19"
        IF kind EQUALS `o 18 r 1(2) any other application` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "an application in an action — (a) includes any application" (the list of what it includes is not closed)
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE -- includes: the three limbs of (2)(a)

-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
§§ `Rule 2 -- general matters and structure of this Order`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `o 18 r 2 division` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 2(2) Division 2`
    `o 18 r 2(3) Division 3`
    `o 18 r 2(4) Division 4`
    `o 18 r 2(5) Division 5`

DECLARE `o 18 r 2 kind of appeal` IS ONE OF
    `o 18 r 2(2) an appeal from the Registrar to the District Judge in proceedings in the State Courts`
    `o 18 r 2(3) an appeal from the District Judge or Magistrate to the General Division`
    `o 18 r 2(4) an appeal from the Registrar to the Judge in proceedings in the General Division`
    `o 18 r 2(5) an appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, an appeal transferred between them, an appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal, or an application to either relating to such an appeal`
    `o 18 r 2 any other appeal`

-- src:1727 | 2. —(1) This Order is subject to any written law on the right to appeal and any requirement to apply for permission to appeal. (2) Division 2 of this Order concerns appeals from the Registrar to the District Judge in proceedings in the State Courts.
@ref O 18 r 2(1) (src:1727)
GIVEN `a written law on the right to appeal or a requirement to apply for permission to appeal applies` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 2(1) this Order gives way to a written law on the right to appeal or on permission to appeal` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law on the right to appeal or a requirement to apply for permission to appeal applies` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent) (the paragraph states a priority and does not say that the Order is otherwise unaffected)

-- src:1727 | 2. —(1) This Order is subject to any written law on the right to appeal and any requirement to apply for permission to appeal. (2) Division 2 of this Order concerns appeals from the Registrar to the District Judge in proceedings in the State Courts.
-- src:1728 | (3) Division 3 of this Order concerns appeals from the District Judge and Magistrate to the General Division.
-- src:1729 | (4) Division 4 of this Order concerns appeals from the Registrar to the Judge in proceedings in the General Division.
-- src:1730 | (5) Division 5 of this Order concerns appeals to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal (including appeals transferred between the Appellate Division and the Court of Appeal), appeals from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal, and applications to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal relating to such appeals.
@ref O 18 r 2(2) to (5) (src:1727-1730)
GIVEN kind IS A `o 18 r 2 kind of appeal`
GIVETH A MAYBE `o 18 r 2 division`
`o 18 r 2 the Division of this Order that concerns the appeal` MEANS
    CONSIDER kind
    WHEN `o 18 r 2(2) an appeal from the Registrar to the District Judge in proceedings in the State Courts` THEN JUST `o 18 r 2(2) Division 2`
    WHEN `o 18 r 2(3) an appeal from the District Judge or Magistrate to the General Division` THEN JUST `o 18 r 2(3) Division 3`
    WHEN `o 18 r 2(4) an appeal from the Registrar to the Judge in proceedings in the General Division` THEN JUST `o 18 r 2(4) Division 4`
    WHEN `o 18 r 2(5) an appeal to the Appellate Division or the Court of Appeal, an appeal transferred between them, an appeal from the Appellate Division to the Court of Appeal, or an application to either relating to such an appeal` THEN JUST `o 18 r 2(5) Division 5`
    WHEN `o 18 r 2 any other appeal` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): paragraphs (2) to (5) say which Division "concerns" four kinds of appeal and say nothing of any other

