§§ `Rule 3 -- when time for appeal starts to run`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1733 | (1A) Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days after the lower Court has heard and determined all other matters in the application, the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the expiry of the 30‑day period, even if the lower Court has directed that submissions on costs be made. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 18 r 3(1A) (src:1733)
`o 18 r 3(1A) the period for the lower Court to determine costs` MEANS Period WITH
    `period length` IS 30
    `period unit` IS Days
    `period direction` IS `After the anchor`

-- src:1732 | 3. —(1) Subject to any written law and paragraphs (1A) and (2), unless the Court otherwise orders, the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal does not start to run until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in an application, including costs. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 18 r 3(1) (src:1732)
GIVEN `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law and paragraphs (1A) and (2)"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        IF `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "does not start to run until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in an application, including costs" (a bar is not an affirmative: after the matters are determined this paragraph does not itself say that the time runs, and the bar's own yes/no question is the function below (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d); fork 18.6))
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not start to run until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in an application, including costs" (time does not yet run: a flat negative)

@ref O 18 r 3(1) (src:1732)
GIVEN `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 3(1) the time for filing an appeal or an application for permission to appeal is still barred from starting to run` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `a written law, paragraph (1A) or paragraph (2) provides otherwise` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): "Subject to any written law and paragraphs (1A) and (2)"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "unless the Court otherwise orders" (an "unless" that is met lifts the bar, so the bar's own question answers no (fork 18.6))
        IF `the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in the application, including costs` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "until after the lower Court has heard and determined all matters in an application, including costs" (the bar has lifted (ruling of 2026-11-05, delegated (d)))
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE --(the bar holds: before the lower Court has heard and determined all matters, including costs)

-- src:1733 | (1A) Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days after the lower Court has heard and determined all other matters in the application, the time for the filing of an appeal or for the filing of an application for permission to appeal starts to run after the expiry of the 30‑day period, even if the lower Court has directed that submissions on costs be made. [S 37/2024 wef 01/02/2024]
@ref O 18 r 3(1A) (src:1733)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE DATE
`o 18 r 3(1A) the date after which the time starts to run where costs are not determined within 30 days` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs AT MOST (`the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` PLUS 30)
        THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days" (costs were determined within 30 days; a figure cannot be a JUST FALSE)
        ELSE JUST (`the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` PLUS 30)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST (`the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` PLUS 30)

@ref O 18 r 3(1A) (src:1733)
GIVEN `the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` IS A DATE
      `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs` IS A MAYBE DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 3(1A) the time starts to run after the expiry of the 30-day period` MEANS
    CONSIDER `the date the lower Court heard and determined the issue of costs`
    WHEN JUST costs THEN
        IF costs AT MOST (`the date the lower Court heard and determined all other matters in the application` PLUS 30)
        THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where the lower Court does not hear and determine the issue of costs within 30 days" (a "where" that is not met, ruling of 2026-11-05 (b); the date function above cannot carry a no, so this yes/no twin does)
        ELSE JUST TRUE
    WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST TRUE

