-- src:1756 | 4. —(1) Subject to paragraph (2), each party is allowed to file only one appeal for each application unless the Court otherwise orders. (2) In the case of a single application pending trial dealing with more than one matter and where permission to appeal is required for one or more of the matters, each party must file a separate notice of appeal for matters which require permission to appeal, and for matters which do not require permission to appeal.
@ref O 18 r 4(1) (src:1756)
GIVEN `the party has already filed an appeal for the application` IS A BOOLEAN
      `paragraph (2) applies` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court has otherwise ordered` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 4(1) the party may file another appeal for the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the party has already filed an appeal for the application`) THEN JUST TRUE
        IF `paragraph (2) applies` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Subject to paragraph (2)"
        IF `the Court has otherwise ordered` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "unless the Court otherwise orders"
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "each party is allowed to file only one appeal for each application"

