§§ `Rule 12 -- withdrawal of appeal or application`
-- ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:1782 | 12. —(1) An appellant may withdraw the appellant’s appeal in relation to all or any of the respondents, and an applicant in an application to the appellate Court may withdraw the applicant’s application in relation to all or any of the parties to the application, at any time before the appeal or application is heard or dealt with (as the case may be), by filing and serving a notice of withdrawal of the appeal or application in Form 34 on all the parties to the appeal or application. (2) Upon the filing of Form 34 and if there are no outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters, the appeal or application is deemed withdrawn in relation to the relevant parties, and if all the parties to the appeal or application consent to the payment of the security for costs to the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be), the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be) must file the document signifying such consent signed by the parties and in such event, the security for costs must be paid to the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be) and any solicitor’s undertaking is discharged.
@ref O 18 r 12(1) (src:1782)
GIVEN `the appeal or application has already been heard or dealt with` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice of withdrawal in Form 34 is filed and served on all the parties` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 12(1) the appellant may withdraw the appeal or the applicant may withdraw the application` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `the appeal or application has already been heard or dealt with` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "at any time before the appeal or application is heard or dealt with" (a period the text fixes in its own words, ruling of 2026-11-05 (a))
        IF `the notice of withdrawal in Form 34 is filed and served on all the parties` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "by filing and serving a notice of withdrawal of the appeal or application in Form 34 on all the parties to the appeal or application"

-- src:1782 | 12. —(1) An appellant may withdraw the appellant’s appeal in relation to all or any of the respondents, and an applicant in an application to the appellate Court may withdraw the applicant’s application in relation to all or any of the parties to the application, at any time before the appeal or application is heard or dealt with (as the case may be), by filing and serving a notice of withdrawal of the appeal or application in Form 34 on all the parties to the appeal or application. (2) Upon the filing of Form 34 and if there are no outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters, the appeal or application is deemed withdrawn in relation to the relevant parties, and if all the parties to the appeal or application consent to the payment of the security for costs to the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be), the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be) must file the document signifying such consent signed by the parties and in such event, the security for costs must be paid to the appellant, the applicant or the respondent (as the case may be) and any solicitor’s undertaking is discharged.
@ref O 18 r 12(2) (src:1782)
GIVEN `Form 34 has been filed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `there are outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 12(2) the appeal or application is deemed withdrawn in relation to the relevant parties` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `Form 34 has been filed` AND (NOT `there are outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters`) THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Upon the filing of Form 34 and if there are no outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

@ref O 18 r 12(2) (src:1782)
GIVEN `the appeal or application is deemed withdrawn` IS A BOOLEAN
      `all the parties consent to the payment of the security for costs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document signifying the consent signed by the parties is filed` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`o 18 r 12(2) the security for costs must be paid and the solicitor's undertaking is discharged` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF (NOT `the appeal or application is deemed withdrawn`) OR (NOT `all the parties consent to the payment of the security for costs`) THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "if all the parties to the appeal or application consent to the payment of the security for costs" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)
        IF `the document signifying the consent signed by the parties is filed` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must file the document signifying such consent signed by the parties and in such event" (an "in such event" that is not met, read as "in the event of" and so as "where" (assumed, not ruled: fork 15.7))

