        IF `there are outstanding issues relating to costs or other matters` THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If there are any such outstanding issues mentioned in paragraph (2)" (an "if" that is not met, read as the text's no: a marginal reading for a lawyer)

