-- src:1800 | 13. —(1) Where the parties in any appeal or application to the appellate Court inform the Registrar that they wish to record a consent judgment or order, the appellate Court may dispense with attendance of the parties and may record the judgment or order in the agreed terms, and the Registrar is to inform the parties accordingly. (2) The appellate Court may give such further orders or directions incidental or consequential to any judgment or order that the appellate Court considers appropriate.
